{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba PAID-GATE.md; cat rehearsal.log; cat paid-plan.sha256'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# judging-v13 paid gate: plan, harness and reading rule (registered before any send; D725, D729, D730)\n     2\t\n     3\t## 1. What is sent\n     4\t\n     5\t`paid_gate.py plan paid-plan.json` builds 12 requests from the stored runs.\n     6\t\n     7\t| Unit | Arm | Members | Evidence shown |\n     8\t|---|---|---|---|\n     9\t| pair-old-1 (09-20: v4 total, v8 Data Center) | joint; separate-v4; separate-v8 | both; one; one | the union of both stored requests' evidence in view (237 items), in every arm |\n    10\t| pair-old-2 (v14, v9) | joint; separate-v14; separate-v9 | as above | 237 |\n    11\t| pair-old-3 (v3, v35) | joint; separate-v3; separate-v35 | as above | 260 |\n    12\t| single-O (old-2 v29, equity commitments) | single | v29 | its own request's (35) |\n    13\t| single-S (old-2 v6, four hyperscalers' 2027 capex) | single | v6 | 31 |\n    14\t| single-E (old-3 v41, FY2028 Vera CPU) | single | v41 | 15 |\n    15\t\n    16\t- **Each request:** judging-v13's system text (`judging-v13-draft.txt`, 4,373 characters); the family header with the exact outcome\n    17\t  keys; the evidence; the themes once. No earlier forecast is shown (D728). The strict v13 schema.\n    18\t- **The model:** poc-v118's re-judging setting (gpt-6-luna, medium effort, 16,000 output tokens).\n    19\t- **Draws:** three per request, so 36 first attempts.\n    20\t- **Retry:** a calculation the checks refuse, or a schema-invalid answer, is retried once with the reasons. A second refusal makes the\n    21\t  unit unresolved.\n    22\t- **The separate arm:** its two answers per pair and draw are merged and checked over the pair's family (C3, C4 across the two).\n    23\t\n    24\t## 2. Spend and stops\n    25\t\n    26\t- **The ledger:** one, at Alex's ceiling (`paid_gate.py send <folder> <ceiling> paid-plan.json` refuses any other ceiling).\n    27\t- **Budget:** the real budget transport and stop gate, which reserve each request's worst case before sending. After a stop, nothing\n    28\t  more is sent, and the remaining units are recorded as not sent.\n    29\t- **Estimate:** about $0.004–0.008 a call, so $0.15–0.30 for 36, plus retries. **Proposed ceiling: $0.50.**\n    30\t- **Sends:** one at a time. Each send has its own archive, so no draw is answered from another.\n    31\t\n    32\t## 3. The $0 rehearsal (`paid_rehearsal.py`, `rehearsal.log`: 16 of 16)\n    33\t\n    34\t- **Clean run:** 36 first attempts, every HTTP body byte-equal to an independently built request, every unit published, the separate\n    35\t  arm reconciled in 9 of 9, the spend settled under the ceiling.\n    36\t- **Paths:**\n    37\t  - a refused calculation is retried, then published;\n    38\t  - two refusals give unresolved;\n    39\t  - a schema-invalid answer is retried;\n    40\t  - two separate answers that each pass alone are refused when reconciled (C3);\n    41\t  - after a ledger stop, nothing more is sent.\n    42\t- **Packets:** 27 packets with the arm hidden. The verdict is computed on synthetic readings: both arms good gives STOP (gain under 3);\n    43\t  a joint gain of 4 gives PASS; one published singleton defect gives STOP; a separate-arm defect alone does not stop; a missing\n    44\t  reading gives INCOMPLETE.\n    45\t\n    46\t## 3b. After council round 47 (`codex-r47.md`)\n    47\t\n    48\t- **[47.1] Reconciliation:** forecasts of the same quantity and scenario with equal recomputed values and bounds are unified before the\n    49\t  family's checks run. The duplicate's derivation is kept in results. Forecasts that differ stay as a conflict. Rehearsed: an agreeing\n    50\t  pair passes, and a disagreeing pair is refused (C4).\n    51\t- **[47.2] One authorization:**\n    52\t  - `paid-plan.sha256` pins the reviewed plan, and the sender refuses any other plan;\n    53\t  - `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/authorization.json` is created exclusively at the first send, so a second launch is refused;\n    54\t  - (unit, arm) pairs are unique.\n    55\t- **[47.3] Every attempt recorded:**\n    56\t  - a `started` line is written before the provider is called;\n    57\t  - checker failures and arithmetic errors are refusals, recorded with the raw answer;\n    58\t  - every planned unit has a final status (`finals.json`), even after an abort;\n    59\t  - a refused reservation never reaches the provider.\n    60\t- **[47.4] Readings validated:** exact packets and cards, two readings (A, B) per card with yes or no and a ground for each question,\n    61\t  and a third reading on every disagreement. Otherwise the verdict is INCOMPLETE.\n    62\t- **[47.5] Packets:**\n    63\t  - the question text and ladder;\n    64\t  - each passage exactly as the request showed it, including those named only in `rests_on`;\n    65\t  - declared figures with renumbered ids, the recomputed outcomes and the recorded assumptions;\n    66\t  - the cards a non-reconciled separate unit has;\n    67\t  - neutral decision labels.\n    68\t- **Rehearsal:** 27 of 27 (`rehearsal.log`). The $0 gate still passes (`gate-run27.txt`: 87 of 87), and the mutants are unchanged.\n    69\t\n    70\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n    71\t\n    72\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n    73\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n    74\t  - Each packet shows the questions, every passage a figure or citation names (as the request showed it), the figures and the cards.\n    75\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. Its cards cannot count as usable.\n    76\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n    77\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n    78\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n    79\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n    80\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n    81\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n    82\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n    83\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n    84\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines):\n    85\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n    86\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n    87\t    singleton answers.\n    88\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n    89\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n    90\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n    91\t\n    92\t## 5. What the result decides\n    93\t\n    94\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n    95\t  step Alex opens.\n    96\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\nPASS  clean: 36 first attempts, no retry  36 attempts\nPASS  clean: every body byte-equal to the planned request  []\nPASS  clean: every unit publishes  \nPASS  clean: the separate arm reconciles in all 9 pairs  \nPASS  clean: spend settled under the ceiling  spent 0.1156\nPASS  packets: 27 packets; no arm word or member prefix in the text  27 packets\nPASS  verdict: both arms usable everywhere: STOP (gain under 3)  \nPASS  verdict: joint 9, separate 5: PASS  5\nPASS  verdict: one published singleton defect: STOP  \nPASS  verdict: a defect in the separate arm alone does not stop  \nPASS  verdict: missing packet: INCOMPLETE  P01: not read\nPASS  verdict: invented card: INCOMPLETE  P01: cards ['v9', 'v999'] are not the unit's ['v14', 'v9']\nPASS  verdict: missing ground: INCOMPLETE  P01 v14 usable: reader A gave no yes/no with a ground\nPASS  verdict: disagreement, no third: INCOMPLETE  P01 v14 usable: the readers disagree and no third reading decides\nPASS  verdict: a disagreement decided by the third reader is complete  \nPASS  separate-agree: equal shared Q3 forecasts are unified, and the pair reconciles  []\nPASS  separate-disagree: different shared Q3 forecasts are refused (C4)  \nPASS  div-zero: recorded and refused (C2), then retried  ['refused', 'publish']\nPASS  reservation: a refused reservation never reaches the provider and is recorded  0 provider calls\nPASS  send refuses no ceiling named  the approved ceiling is None (Alex names it); refused\nPASS  send refuses a changed plan  the plan is not the reviewed one (sha256 differs); refused\nPASS  send refuses a used authorization  /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b600\nPASS  retry: a refused calculation is retried once with its errors and then publishes  ['refused', 'publish']\nPASS  unresolved: two refusals make the unit unresolved  \nPASS  format: a schema-invalid answer is refused, then retried  ['format invalid', 'answered']\nPASS  separate: two answers that each pass alone are refused when reconciled (C3)  refused\nPASS  ledger-stop: after the ledger stops, nothing more is sent  5 attempts, 31 not sent\n27 of 27 checks pass\n6f81dae5bd76debae944002f9a1421cb094cb05bbb36b4f4545bcb251db28478\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
