{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport json,pathlib,paid_gate as pg\np=json.loads(pathlib.Path('\\\\''paid-plan.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nclass Mem:\n    fs={}\n    def __init__(self,p): self.p=p\n    def __truediv__(self,k): return Mem(self.p+'\\\\''/'\\\\''+k)\n    def write_text(self,txt): self.fs[self.p]=txt\ng=pg.Gate.__new__(pg.Gate)\ng.out=Mem('\\\\''out'\\\\'')\ng.ledger=None\nlog=[]\ndef interrupt(it,draw):\n    log.append({'\\\\''unit'\\\\'':it['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],'\\\\''arm'\\\\'':it['\\\\''arm'\\\\''],'\\\\''draw'\\\\'':draw,'\\\\''status'\\\\'':'\\\\''started'\\\\''})\n    log.append({'\\\\''unit'\\\\'':it['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],'\\\\''arm'\\\\'':it['\\\\''arm'\\\\''],'\\\\''draw'\\\\'':draw,'\\\\''status'\\\\'':'\\\\''answered'\\\\'','\\\\''decision'\\\\'':'\\\\''refused'\\\\''})\n    raise KeyboardInterrupt('\\\\''interrupted before the retry finished'\\\\'')\ng.unit=interrupt\ntry:\n    g.run(p)\nexcept KeyboardInterrupt:\n    pass\nfs=Mem.fs\nprint('\\\\''paid unit has trace, final, results readable:'\\\\'',log,json.loads(fs['\\\\''out/finals.json'\\\\''])['\\\\''pair-old-1|joint|1'\\\\''],'\\\\''out/results.json'\\\\'' in fs)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport json,pathlib,paid_gate as pg\np=json.loads(pathlib.Path('\\\\''paid-plan.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nclass Mem:\n    fs={}\n    def __init__(self,p): self.p=p\n    def __truediv__(self,k): return Mem(self.p+'\\\\''/'\\\\''+k)\n    def write_text(self,txt): self.fs[self.p]=txt\ng=pg.Gate.__new__(pg.Gate)\ng.out=Mem('\\\\''out'\\\\'')\ng.ledger=None\nlog=[]\ndef interrupt(it,draw):\n    log.append({'\\\\''unit'\\\\'':it['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],'\\\\''arm'\\\\'':it['\\\\''arm'\\\\''],'\\\\''draw'\\\\'':draw,'\\\\''status'\\\\'':'\\\\''started'\\\\''})\n    log.append({'\\\\''unit'\\\\'':it['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],'\\\\''arm'\\\\'':it['\\\\''arm'\\\\''],'\\\\''draw'\\\\'':draw,'\\\\''status'\\\\'':'\\\\''answered'\\\\'','\\\\''decision'\\\\'':'\\\\''refused'\\\\''})\n    raise KeyboardInterrupt('\\\\''interrupted before the retry finished'\\\\'')\ng.unit=interrupt\ntry:\n    g.run(p)\nexcept KeyboardInterrupt:\n    pass\nfs=Mem.fs\nprint('\\\\''paid unit has trace, final, results readable:'\\\\'',log,json.loads(fs['\\\\''out/finals.json'\\\\''])['\\\\''pair-old-1|joint|1'\\\\''],'\\\\''out/results.json'\\\\'' in fs)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"paid unit has trace, final, results readable: [{'unit': 'pair-old-1', 'arm': 'joint', 'draw': 1, 'status': 'started'}, {'unit': 'pair-old-1', 'arm': 'joint', 'draw': 1, 'status': 'answered', 'decision': 'refused'}] {'decision': 'not sent'} False\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"NOT READY\n\n1. **Reconciliation can bias the separate arm in either direction.** Two independently accepted Q4 forecasts of $127.12B failed reconciliation because one recomputed as `127.12000000000002`. When I made the values equal, the merge replaced the separate Data Center answer’s unsupported estimate with the total-revenue answer’s derivation. Use a fixed numeric equivalence rule for reconciliation, and have blind readers assess each card against its original derivation. [Merge](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:220)\n\n2. **A run can still pass with an unsent request.** A reservation refusal is recorded as `transport`, but the verdict only checks labels beginning with `not sent` and never reads the run’s attempt records. A replay with the last singleton unsent returned `PASS`. An interruption after a recorded answer also left that unit marked `not sent` and produced no `results.json` for packet generation. Track actual dispatch and completion separately, then derive final statuses and completeness from that record. [Attempt handling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:154) · [Verdict](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:442)\n\n3. **The blind packets still omit answers and expose the arm.** My packet replay omitted the first attempt and the separate answer’s original derivation. Its assumption record still printed `v14.q4f`, revealing the separate arm despite the figure renumbering. Include every attempt or explicit failure, and apply the same neutral ID mapping to figures, cards and assumption records. [Packet builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:362)\n\n4. **Readings can pass without grounds or a link to this run.** JSON `null` passes the ground check because it is converted to the string `\"None\"`. The verdict accepts a supplied packet key without verifying it against the run, and packet generation can reshuffle and overwrite that key. Freeze the packet inventory and key before reading, bind them to the run, and require nonempty text grounds tied to the packet. [Packet key and reading validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:413)"}}
